{"path":"io/basic_istream/~basic_istream","title":"std::basic_istream<CharT,Traits>::~basic_istream","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_istream&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>~basic_istream","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_istream/~basic_istream","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Destructs the input stream.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">virtual</span> ~basic_istream<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Destructs the input stream.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>This destructor does not perform any operation on the underlying streambuffer (<code>rdbuf()</code>): the destructors of the derived input streams such as <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_ifstream\">std::basic_ifstream</a></span> and <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istringstream\">std::basic_istringstream</a></span> are responsible for calling the destructors of the streambuffers.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;sstream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> print_stringbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf\"><span class=\"kw1741\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streambuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> p<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istream\"><span class=\"kw1744\">std::<span class=\"me2\">istream</span></span></a> buf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>p<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// buf shares the buffer with s1</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    buf <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span> <span class=\"co1\">// calls the destructor of buf. p remains unaffected</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_istringstream\"><span class=\"kw1752\">std::<span class=\"me2\">istringstream</span></span></a> s1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"10 20\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    print_stringbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span>s1.<span class=\"me1\">rdbuf</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    s1 <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;&gt;</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">','</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> n <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>10,20</code></pre> \n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_istream","title":"std::basic_istream"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_istream<CharT,Traits>::~basic_istream","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Destructs the input stream."},{"label":"Notes","note":"This destructor does not perform any operation on the underlying streambuffer (rdbuf()): the destructors of the derived input streams such as…"},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":98,"codeBlockCount":2}
